<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Names</h1>
<p>A name must be 3 to 14 letters long, with no spaces, digits or other signs, 
and the game turns down common words and names on its list of banned 
names. Beyond that, these are the house rules:
</p><p>When picking a name for your character keep in mind that Valhalla has a medieval fantasy theme and choose your name accordingly. John for example may have been a name in use in the middle ages but it does little to add to the atmosphere of a fantasy game.
</p><p>The following are examples of bad name choices:
</p><p>George, Mark, John, Susan etc. These are modern, and most likely in use as a mob name (see below).
</p><p>Compound names that include first and surname, a title, or a phrase. Ericthemagicuser, Georgewashington, and Dieorcdie are examples.
</p><p>Do not make names that have more than one capital letter. WhiteWolf, SleepyDwarf, and SnInkEr are examples of these.
</p><p>Excessively long names or names that are nothing more than a string of letters. Asdfghjklqwerty is one such example, remember this is a text based game.
</p><p>Obscene, offensive or suggestive names will not be accepted.
</p><p>Names that are obviously out of genre such as coprocessor, television, spaceship.
</p><p>Obvious product names are not permitted as character names. Pepsi, Kleenex, and Microsoft are examples.
</p><p>Titles as names are not permitted as character names. King, President, and Empress are examples. Many are likely to also be mobile names, so the same risk applies (see below).
</p><p>We ask you do not name a character after a mobile, object or a command on the MUD. Understand if you do, you do so at your risk, code changes could cause such a character to become corrupted or deleted. If this occurs, there will be no compensation for characters lost.
</p><p>The Administration reserves the right to deny the use of any name without compensation. This means that if you make a character and level it up, an administrator can ask you to delete the character and start over. We realize characters created prior to 2003 were made before the naming conventions were instituted. These have been 'grandfathered' in and may continue to be played.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
